  Cache lifetime is exactly the page's lifetime. Nothing is written to [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m, [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m, or a readable
  cookie — which is what keeps the stale-identity failure from section 1's alternative off the table entirely.

  Does this look right so far? Next sections are the backend contract (including one cross-origin wrinkle I want to
  flag), error handling, and testing + tooling.

