  [1mThe audit clause[0m (this is your original "track who logged in", and it's the entire tracking deliverable): the server
  records every login [3mattempt[0m — [38;5;153muserId[39m on success or the attempted username on failure, timestamp, outcome, source IP,
  user agent. Recording failures matters more than recording successes; a log of only successful logins can't show you a
  brute-force attempt.

